cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Radar Micro-Doppler AI: End-to-End Helicopter Classification with Classical, Quantum, and Deep Learning"
authors:
  - family-names: Agnihotri
    given-names: Vikas
date-released: "2026-09-05"
url: "https://github.com/bukac82/radar-microdoppler-ai"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  An end-to-end AI pipeline for helicopter micro-Doppler signature classification
  using Classical ML (SVM, Random Forest, XGBoost, k-NN), Quantum ML (QK-SVM, VQC),
  and Deep Learning (ResNet CNN, Bi-LSTM, Spectrogram Transformer).
  The project includes physics-based dataset generation, robustness testing under
  AWGN and adversarial attacks, open-set recognition for unknown aerial targets,
  and model explainability via SHAP and Grad-CAM.
keywords:
  - radar
  - micro-doppler
  - helicopter classification
  - quantum machine learning
  - deep learning
  - open-set recognition
  - adversarial robustness
  - explainable AI
